                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Slow tutorial that starts of all blurry as you need to pick up your eye. Your vision will get damaged when you get attacked, not fun.\nThe tutorial itself is not very good. It asks you to buy and equip two abilities. You can buy any ability that you can afford but it wants you to buy and equip two specific ones. So instead of just locking all other abilities for the tutorial or let the player pick what they want to you get this.\nThe gameplay itself is just running around back and forth in a maze and pick up objects and do puzzles while being chased by one special enemy that can very easily kill you if it gets close enough. Other enemies are easier to deal with.\nIf you start the game with all abilities unlocked then you can softlock the tutorial depending on what abilities you equipped.\nYour only way of defending yourself is limited.\nYour flashlights battery drains while you use it and recharges when off. If you use it until it runs out you are in complete darkness for a some seconds.\nThe game is dark even when you have color mode. The noir mode has been done better in other games.",
